  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 5. Reconstruction question: is the linear map |A> -> <v_new(params) (x) e1 | A> injective on the span of ALL hw vectors\n   (states mixing several weights allowed)? Exact, at finite twist. Rank = # hw vectors minus the missed ones means the kernel is exactly\n   the missed irreps: any hw |A> with no component there is fixed uniquely (normalization included) by its overlaps. ---- *)\nModule[{hwAll = Flatten[Table[hwC[nu], {nu, hwWtsC}], 1], slices, P, P2},\n    slices = Transpose[Table[Partition[w, dC][[All, 1]], {w, hwAll}]];\n    P = Together /@ (vnewC . slices);\n    P2 = Together /@ (vnew2C . slices);\n    Grid[\n        {\n            {\"site rep\", lamC},\n            {\"# hw vectors of V (x) V (all weights)\", Length[hwAll]},\n            {\"rank of the overlap map, old family v_new\", MatrixRank[coefMatC[P]]},\n            {\"rank, old + determinant family\", MatrixRank[Join[coefMatC[P], coefMatC[P2]]]},\n            {\"hw weights where the per-weight rank < multiplicity (missed)\", Select[rowsHW2C, #[[5]] < #[[2]] &][[All, 1]]}\n        },\n        Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left\n    ]\n]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
